model { extend basalt.deployment { metadata { constraint "Deployment backend acceptance counts direct and pooled runtime client backends per logical database only after desired runtime readiness. Unknown visibility is a failed observation; release-only signed readiness and boot revalidation precede the unchanged 90-second convergence window within a 270-second overall operation counted from the readiness receipt. The existing two-minute verifier wrapper reserves five seconds for retention and teardown. Readiness asks again every five seconds while the controller refuses with 503 or 409, for up to 510 seconds: 330 for the controller object to adopt the uploaded code, then the unchanged 180-second startup budget. Any other refusal fails at once. The receipt records how often readiness was refused, the last refusal, and whether the controller object had adopted the code." } } }
